"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/netherlands_paperback_writer.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"713,717\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paperback Writer single artwork \u2013 Netherlands\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/netherlands_paperback_writer.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/japan_paperback_writer/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Paperback Writer single artwork - Japan\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-580x578.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-960x957.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-768x766.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9592\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/japan_paperback_writer/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,997\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paperback Writer single artwork \u2013 Japan\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_paperback_writer-960x957.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><h2><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Top_Of_The_Pops_appearance\"></span>Top Of The Pops appearance<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2><p>Although by June 1966 it had been running for over two years, The Beatles had never before appeared live on the BBC music show <em>Top Of The Pops</em>. They had pre-recorded exclusive performances in BBC studios, or sent promotional clips to be played on the show. <span id=\"more-224\"></span></p><p>That changed on this day, with a studio performance of new single &#8216;Paperback Writer&#8217;. The Beatles had agreed two days previously, when manager <a href=\"/people/brian-epstein/\">Brian Epstein</a> passed on a request from <em>Top Of The Pops</em> producer Johnnie Stewart. Unusually, on this occasion The Beatles agreed.</p><p>The group arrived at BBC Television Centre at 2.30pm for a rehearsal for the camera, and to pose for publicity photographs and conduct press interviews. More rehearsals followed between 4.15pm and 5.30, and from 6.30pm to 7pm.</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/1966-photos/the-beatles/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-22252\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSI3OTAiIGhlaWdodD0iNTIxIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgNzkwIDUyMSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"22252\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1966-photos/the-beatles/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-scaled.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"2560,1687\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Beatles on Top Of The Pops, 16 June 1966\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-960x633.jpg\" data-src=\"/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-960x633.jpg\" alt=\"The Beatles on Top Of The Pops, 16 June 1966\" width=\"790\" height=\"521\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-22252\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-960x633.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-580x382.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-200x132.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-768x506.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-1536x1012.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/660616-beatles-top-of-the-pops_01-2048x1350.jpg 2048w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 790px) 100vw, 790px\" /></a></p><p>The live broadcast took place between 7.30pm and 8pm on BBC One. The Beatles were the final act to appear, and mimed to both &#8216;Paperback Writer&#8217; and its b-side, <a href=\"/songs/rain/\">&#8216;Rain&#8217;</a>. They were introduced by host Pete Murray.</p><p>The Beatles&#8217; only appearance on <em>Top Of The Pop</em>s was, with the exception of the worldwide satellite transmission of <a href=\"/songs/all-you-need-is-love/\">&#8216;All You Need Is Love&#8217;</a> on <a href=\"/1967/06/25/the-beatles-on-our-world-all-you-need-is-love/\">25 June 1967</a>, their final live television appearance as a group.</p><h2><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Live_performances\"></span>Live performances<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2><p>&#8216;Paperback Writer&#8217; was performed during The Beatles&#8217; last tour in 1966. It was the penultimate song played at their final concert on <a href=\"/1966/08/29/candlestick-park-san-francisco-final-concert/\">29 August</a>, at San Francisco&#8217;s Candlestick Park.</p><blockquote><div>We were just a little dance-hall band and we never really thought of augmenting ourselves. We thought, &#8216;Well, we can&#8217;t. We&#8217;ll do it to the best of our ability until the point where we can&#8217;t really do it, and then we&#8217;ll miss it out.&#8217; So around this time we were starting to miss out a lot of record tracks on live shows.</p><p>&#8216;Paperback Writer&#8217;, for instance, was all double-tracked, and it sounded pretty crummy on stage. So what we did with it, in the American tour at least, was get to the point where it was particularly bad, and then we&#8217;d do our &#8216;Elvis legs&#8217; and wave to the crowds, and they&#8217;d all scream and it would cover that. As <a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul</a> has said, the screaming did cover a lot of worrying moments.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/george-harrison/\">George Harrison</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><div class=\"fab-forum-link\"><a href=\"/fab-forum/the-songs/paperback-writer/\">Discuss &#8216;Paperback Writer&#8217; on the Fab Forum \u00bb</a></div><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/paperback-writer/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/songs/paperback-writer/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></span></div>",
